# pots v1.4 — NEGATIVE. A blood pressure observation carrying no component.
#
# This is the whole of pots:BloodPressureMeasurementShape's Violation surface:
# one constraint, sh:path fhir:component with sh:minCount 1. A blood pressure
# with no components is a record that says a reading was taken and does not say
# what it was -- worse than a missing record, because it occupies the slot a real
# reading would fill and reads as data.
#
# EXACTLY ONE CONSTRAINT FIRES:
#   pots:BloodPressureMeasurementShape / path fhir:component
#   / MinCountConstraintComponent
#
# THE REALISTIC PRODUCER ERROR is putting the numbers where they do not belong,
# so that is what this fixture does. It carries fhir:valueQuantity directly on
# the observation -- the shape a HEART RATE takes -- rather than nesting the two
# values under fhir:component. A converter written for the single-valued case and
# reused for blood pressure emits precisely this: a plausible-looking node whose
# systolic reading has quietly become the observation's own value and whose
# diastolic has been dropped. Nothing in the shape rejects the stray
# fhir:valueQuantity; the missing component is what makes it invalid, and the
# record is wrong in a way a reader skimming the Turtle would not notice.
#
# pots:secondsSinceStand is Info-severity and correct, so it contributes nothing
# to the verdict either way.
#
# Fully synthetic.

@prefix pots: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/pots/v1#> .
@prefix fhir: <http://hl7.org/fhir/> .
@prefix loinc: <http://loinc.org/rdf#> .
@prefix ucum: <http://unitsofmeasure.org/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:uuid:p0t5-0005-4a00-8000-00000000bp20> a pots:BloodPressureMeasurement ;
    fhir:code loinc:8480-6 ;
    fhir:valueQuantity [
        fhir:value "118.0"^^xsd:double ;
        fhir:unit "mmHg" ;
        fhir:code ucum:mm-Hg
    ] ;
    pots:secondsSinceStand "0.0"^^xsd:double .
